mode: "100644"
text: "# The LINES framework — text posts that earn the read\n\nA text post is built line by line, and the first line is ~80% of the job. Each letter is a gate; most weak posts\nfail at L (soft opener) or N (a wall of text, or the opposite — over-decorated AI-slop formatting).\n\n## L — Lead with the line that earns the tap\nThe first ~140-210 chars (the mobile \"see more\" fold) are a **mini-post**: write the first line as if it's the\nonly line anyone reads, because for most it is.\n- **Front-load the insight** — a bold claim, a specific result, a surprising stat (a true one), a contrarian take,\n  or a sharp observation. Never open with \"I'm excited to announce…\", a greeting, or a flat question.\n- Design for the **mobile** cutoff; preview how the feed renders it.\n\n## I — Isolate one idea\nA post is **one** clear idea/story/take — not an essay. Ruthless focus; if you're making three points, it's three\nposts. **Match length to the content type and platform** (LinkedIn ~1,300-1,900 for depth, <500 for a take; X\nbrief; Threads ~500; Bluesky ~300) — not a generic number. Structure (hook → turn → payoff → CTA), not character\ncount, does the work.\n\n## N — Negative space\n- **White space = oxygen** — short 1-2 sentence paragraphs, line breaks between thoughts; kill the wall of text\n  (it lifts reading time ~20%).\n- **But don't over-format.** The Unicode-bold-everywhere, emoji/checkmark-per-line, rigid-template look reads as\n  AI slop in 2026 and gets scrolled. One emphasis at most; keep key terms plain (searchable + screen-reader safe).\n  Restraint beats decoration.\n\n## E — Earn the read\nThe body **delivers on the first line's promise** — a real insight, story, or value, one point per paragraph, in\na human brand voice (not corporate, not template). No formatting trick saves a post with no real idea, and the\nagent never fabricates the idea, a stat, or a story. **Native over external links** (link in comments where the\nplatform punishes outbound).\n\n## S — Spark a reply\nEnd on a strong last line + a **genuine, specific engagement driver** — a real question (\"what am I missing?\"), an\ninvited counter-take, or an open loop. Never \"comment YES / like & share\" (engagement-bait, suppressed). Optimize\nfor **comments/saves/dwell**, not likes. Then route platform specifics to `linkedin-post-writer` / `threads-post`\n/ X / `caption-writer` / `thread-writer`; **WoopSocial publishes** to supported platforms (the human posts to\nadvisory ones).\n"
